# What this plugin will not do

One entry, and it is the list of what this plugin writes rather than a single
claim. Two of its three kinds say which of the two states they are in and the
first does not, so the entry passes the leg that asks the question once per
heading on a marker belonging to a different kind. Recorded in #57 so the leg
about issues is not the one that trips.

## What it writes, and where

Three kinds of thing, and no fourth.

The subtitle file, next to the media file or in the item's metadata folder,
following the library's own setting for where the server saves subtitles. #25.

Temporary audio, extracted from the item so a backend has something to work
from, in a directory this plugin owns. Collecting what a dead process orphaned
is decided and not yet built. #11 and #21.

Its own configuration, where the server puts plugin data. Held today, in the
sense that the server writes that file and nothing in this plugin reaches the
location. #42.

## When this list is checked against the code

The closing section, which is about the list rather than a limit in it.
